.TH "WORDEXP" "3" "" "pstring 1.5" "pstring manual"
.SH NAME
wordexp \- API reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include <wordexp.h>\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBtypedef struct pstrexpand_trim_t {
    const pstring_t *value;
    pstring_t *pattern;
    int suffix;
    int greedy;
} pstrexpand_trim_t;\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBtypedef int(pstrexpand_fn)(
    void *dst, void *src, int flags, int kind, void *user
);\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBint pstrexpand(
    pstrarray_t *dst, pstring_t *src, int flags, pstrexpand_fn *cb
);\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBint pstrexpand_with(
    pstrarray_t *dst, pstring_t *src, int flags, pstrexpand_fn *cb, void *user
);\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBint pstrexpand_default_cb(
    void *dst, void *src, int flags, int kind, void *user
);\fR
.fi
.SH REFERENCE
.SS pstrexpand_trim_t
.PP
Payload passed as \fBsrc\fR to a callback invoked with kind ==
\fBPSTREXPAND_TRIM\fR, used by the \fB${var#pattern}\fR family of
parameter\-expansion operators. \fBvalue\fR holds the variable's current
value; \fBpattern\fR holds the (unexpanded) glob pattern text; \fBsuffix\fR
distinguishes \fB%\fR/\fB%%\fR (trim from the end) from \fB#\fR/\fB##\fR (trim from
the start); \fBgreedy\fR distinguishes the doubled \fB##\fR/\fB%%\fR form
(longest match) from the single \fB#\fR/\fB%\fR form (shortest match).
.SS pstrexpand_fn
.PP
Callback used for the \fBwordexp\fR shell expansion.
.SS pstrexpand
.PP
Performs word expansion using the default callback.
.SS pstrexpand_with
.PP
Performs word expansion using the provided callback.
.SS pstrexpand_default_cb
.PP
Default callback used for \fBwordexp\fR shell expansion.
